<title>USA: U.S. Treasury's year bill seen at avg 5.31 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury's year bill seen at avg 5.31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's sale of $19.25 billion in year bills is likely to produce an average rate of 5.31 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the auction is 1300 EST/1800 GMT. Results are expected around 1345 EST/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>In when-issued trade at around 1250 EST/1750 GMT, year bill rates were quoted at 5.3075 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
